autiful candlelit setting of St Mary Le Strand Church in the heart of London</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"block\">\n      <h3>Featuring</h3>\n      <p>\n        Warren Mailley-Smith (piano)<br><br>\n         <div class=\"programme-card\">\n      <h3>Programme</h3>\n      <p class=\"programme-note\"></p>\n      <div class=\"programme-list\" style=\"--prog-rows:4\">\n        <div class=\"programme-item\">\n          <span class=\"programme-num\">1</span>\n          <span>\n            <span class=\"entry-title\">  24.07.26 Mozart - Adagio for Strings, Beethoven - 'Emperor' Piano Concerto No. 5</span>\n          </span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"programme-item\">\n          <span class=\"programme-num\">2</span>\n          <span>\n            <span class=\"entry-title\"> 18.09.26 Holst - St Paul's Suite in C major (Op. 29, No. 2), Beethoven Piano Concerto No. 1</span>\n          </span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"programme-item\">\n          <span class=\"programme-num\">3</span>\n          <span>\n            <span class=\"entry-title\">23.10.26 Mozart - Divertimento in B flat major, Beethoven Piano Concerto no. 2</span>\n          </span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"programme-item\">\n          <span class=\"programme-num\">4</span>\n          <span>\n            <span class=\"entry-title\">13.11.26 Mozart - Eine kleine Nachtmusik, Beethoven - Piano Concerto No. 3</span>\n          </span>\n        </div>\n        Warren Mailley-Smith has captivated audiences nationwide with his expressive playing, effortless technique, and magnetic stage presence. In 2015, he gained international recognition for his remarkable feat of performing the complete solo piano works of Chopin from memory—an achievement that speaks volumes of his artistry and dedication.<br>\n        Round off your evening with dinner or drinks at one of the many nearby restaurants and bars, making this a perfect cultural night out in the heart of London.\n      </p>\n